(ned -- GO TO ZERO: the common start pose for every calibration section.)
(Puck centre from StartPuck, tip 5 mm above the measured top, head at the)
(CURRENT A and C zeros, #3069 and #3070 -- so as calibration corrects them)
(this pose follows, and A/C never get driven back to a stale zero.)
(Rotations happen ONLY with the tool clear above the puck.)

o<cal_goto_zero> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  #<safe>  = 5.0        (operator 2026-08-03: 5 mm for every cal routine)
  #<clear> = 5.0        (tip height above the top, operator spec)
  (non-probing traverse, 5x -- matches the rest of the C path)
  #<f_tr>  = 2500.0

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, GOTO ZERO: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, GOTO ZERO: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  G90
  (Rise to clearance FIRST, then travel and straighten in ONE move with Z)
  (held fixed. Operator 2026-08-03: "its completely safe to keep Z fixed,)
  (move in Y and rotate (even simultaneously)". Z never descends until the)
  (head is upright and over centre, so the swing has nothing under it.)
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<f_tr>]
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> A#3069 C#3070 F[#<f_tr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_tr>]
  (PRINT, GOTO ZERO: at puck centre #<cx> #<cy>, tip #<clear> mm above the top, A0 C0.)

o<cal_goto_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
